  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let $R$ be the relation on the set $R$ of all real numbers, defined by $a R b$ If $|a-b| \\leq 1$. Then, $R$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "A39Tt",
      "text": "reflexive and symmetric only",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Lg1PH",
      "text": "reflexive and transitive only",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "U64r3",
      "text": "equivalence",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gPa8H",
      "text": "None of the above",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since, $|a-a|=0 \\leq 1,$ so $a R a, \\forall a \\in R$ $\\therefore R$ is reflexive. Now, $a R b \\Rightarrow|a-b| \\leq 1 \\Rightarrow|b-a| \\leq 1 \\Rightarrow b R a$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore R$ is symmetric. But $R$ is not transitive as\r\n\r\n$1 R 2,2 R 3$ but $1 \\not R^{\\prime} 3$\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n[\\because|1-3|=2>1]\r\n\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
